<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Neo-Destour</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1934–1964</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Neo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/destour">Destour</a> was a Tunisian nationalist party founded at Ksar Hellal in March 1934 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habib-bourguiba">Habib Bourguiba</a> and other young members who broke with the Destour. Building a mass organisation with trade-union support, it led the struggle that won independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1956 and became the ruling party of the republic. It was renamed the Socialist Destourian Party in 1964.</p></div>
